I’m using the `plan-pm` skill’s own instructions so I can describe its exact handoff and output without changing the repository.
## Skill

Use **`$plan-pm #3`**.

It consumes the graded `INTAKE.md` row and autonomously writes the full product requirements document. It only pauses for unresolved questions or a critical/breaking product decision.

## What it produces

One PRD containing:

- Product objective
- Out-of-scope boundaries
- Features with permanent F-IDs and acceptance criteria
- User-visible error and edge cases
- Open questions
- Reserved sections for the later engineering plan and implementation tickets

It also records dependencies, validates the PRD’s structure, and marks backlog row 3 as `in-progress` with its PRD reference.

## Where it goes

The PRD is created at:

`features/planned/prd-[next-number]-[feature-slug]/prd-[next-number]-[feature-slug].md`

For example:

`features/planned/prd-4-team-notifications/prd-4-team-notifications.md`

The exact number and slug are determined when the skill runs. No files were written.
